---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Mark from '../../components/Mark.astro';
import '../../styles/detail.css';
const mailto = "mailto:manuel@triarc.ch?subject=Consulting%20%E2%80%93%20confidential%20enquiry&body=Business%3A%0AWhat%20it%20is%20about%3A%0ATimeframe%3A%0A";
---
<Base
  title="Operational consulting for hospitality & hotels — by working professionals | Triarc"
  description="Hands-on consulting from a worldwide network of people who still work in hotels and restaurants every day: front office, kitchen, F&B, housekeeping, patisserie. Matched to your house and the level you want, absolutely discreet — and no six-figure mandate."
  lang="en"
  crumb="Consulting"
  altHref="/beratung"
  hreflang={{ de: '/beratung', en: '/en/beratung' }}
>
  <main id="main" class="detail" style="--accent: var(--gold); --accent-wash: color-mix(in srgb, var(--gold) 7%, transparent);">
    <section class="instrument-hero">
      <div>
        <Mark size={76} />
        <p class="d-eyebrow"><span class="roman">II</span>Operational consulting · hands-on</p>
        <h1 class="d-h1">Consulting<span class="stop">.</span></h1>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Service II of III</p>
        <p class="role">Not a consultant off the shelf.<br />A professional from your own trade.</p>
        <p class="hero-intro">The first step is admitting you need help. The second is getting the right kind: whoever comes to you still works in the business today — in a hotel, in a kitchen, at a front desk, somewhere in the world. Matched to your house and to the level you actually want to run — and discreet as a matter of course.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn" href={mailto}>Enquire in confidence <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn-ghost" href="#professionals">Who comes to you</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="trust-strip">
      <span class="who">By the founders <strong>Manuel &amp; Lalaine Bänziger</strong></span>
      <span class="items"><span>Kitchen &amp; F&amp;B</span><span>Front office &amp; reception</span><span>20+ years each, international</span><span>Worldwide network of working professionals</span><span>Discreet as standard</span></span>
    </section>

    <section class="split reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">The first step</p>
        <p class="pull">Admitting that you need help.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="body">In this trade that is the hardest part. Anyone running a house has learned to solve problems alone — which is exactly why so much is left too long. Asking for help feels like an admission.</p>
        <p class="body">Discretion is standard here, not an add-on: the enquiry, the visit and the findings stay in the house, and we never list you as a reference. If you prefer, the professional on site is simply someone lending a hand.</p>
        <p class="body">And it is not a six-figure mandate. No deck that ends up in a drawer — just someone who works a few days at your house and with you, in the daily operation, and leaves once it runs the way you want it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="block reveal" id="check">
      <div class="block-head">
        <h2 class="section-kicker">Where does it hurt?</h2>
        <p class="pull">Tick whatever sounds familiar.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="body" style="max-width:44rem; margin:-20px 0 30px;">No form, no address, no newsletter. Whatever you tick lands in a prepared e-mail — sending it is still your decision.</p>
      <form class="check" id="check-form">
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="Food cost adds up on paper but not in the bank." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">Food cost adds up on paper but not in the bank.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="The menu has grown; the margin has not." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">The menu has grown; the margin has not.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="The same argument about the rota, every week." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">The same argument about the rota, every week.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="Handovers between reception, kitchen and service get lost." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">Handovers between reception, kitchen and service get lost.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="The team turns over faster than we can train people." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">The team turns over faster than we can train people.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="A head-of role is open — or about to be." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">A head-of role is open — or about to be.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="We only know how the month went at the end of it." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">We only know how the month went at the end of it.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="The systems cost money, but nobody uses them fully." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">The systems cost money, but nobody uses them fully.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="The hygiene records are written the night before the inspection." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">The hygiene records are written the night before the inspection.</span></label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox" value="The concept no longer fits the guest who actually walks in." /><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="txt">The concept no longer fits the guest who actually walks in.</span></label></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="check-foot">
          <a class="btn" id="check-send" href={mailto} data-subject="Consulting – confidential enquiry" data-intro="This is where it hurts:" data-none="Nothing ticked? Just write what is on your mind.">Prepare the enquiry <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <p class="check-note" id="check-count" aria-live="polite">Nothing selected — you can simply write instead.</p>
        </div>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section class="block reveal" id="professionals">
      <div class="block-head">
        <h2 class="section-kicker">Who comes to you</h2>
        <p class="pull">Your problem. Exactly the right professional.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="body" style="max-width:44rem; margin:-20px 0 34px;">Not a consultant looking in from outside — someone who knows the shift because they still work it. You will never get a consultant here who isn’t still working in hospitality themselves. Whoever comes to you had the same problem in their own house last week — we find them in a worldwide network of practitioners, not on a consultants' roster.</p>
      <div class="cap-grid">
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Front office &amp; reception</h3><p>A working front office manager takes on your front desk — arrival, reservations, handovers, and the system work from Opera to the daily shift handover.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Kitchen &amp; production</h3><p>An executive chef who still stands in it daily walks your stations, mise en place, menu and costing with you.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">03</span><h3>F&amp;B &amp; service</h3><p>A working F&amp;B manager looks at service, workflows, the menu and the numbers behind them — in live service, not on paper.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">04</span><h3>Housekeeping</h3><p>A practising head of housekeeping checks standards, timings and staffing — where a house’s rating is actually decided.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">05</span><h3>Patisserie &amp; bakery</h3><p>A patissier or baker who still produces takes on your production: recipes, workflows, shelf life, yield.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">06</span><h3>Operations, numbers &amp; systems</h3><p>Costing, food cost, labour ratio — and the question of which systems a house really needs and which it merely pays for. Vendor-neutral.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">07</span><h3>Openings &amp; concept</h3><p>From the idea to a working operation: concept, costing basis, workflows, building the team — accompanied through the first service.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">08</span><h3>Leadership &amp; team</h3><p>Building teams, coaching leaders and training management and crew. So that what was introduced is still lived afterwards.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="nachweis reveal" id="level">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">At your level</p>
        <h2>It has to fit your house.</h2>
        <p>There is no point sending a five-star F&amp;B manager into a house that wants to run mountain hospitality with an honest, homely streak. A good concept is one that fits the house, the guest and the team — not one that imitates a tier nobody asked for. We choose the professional to fit your operation, not our brochure.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="doc-list">
          <p class="lbl">What we ask first</p>
          <li>Which house do you run — and which one do you want to run?</li>
          <li>Who is the guest you actually serve today?</li>
          <li>What level does the team want, and can it carry?</li>
          <li>What is realistic on the budget?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block reveal">
      <h2 class="section-kicker">How it runs</h2>
      <p class="pull">The shape of an engagement.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><span class="n">1</span><h3>A conversation in confidence</h3><p>You say where it hurts. We say who from our circle fits — and whether we are the right people at all.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="n">2</span><h3>Working the shift</h3><p>The professional stands in it with you — kitchen, service, reception, housekeeping, office — and runs the numbers in parallel.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="n">3</span><h3>Implementing on the floor</h3><p>Findings, measures and the rollout at every level alongside you — until the team can hold it without us.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="assurance">
        <span>Discretion as standard — enquiry, visit and findings stay in the house</span>
        <span>Working practitioners only, never career consultants — worldwide</span>
        <span>No six-figure mandate; a clear scope instead of open-ended day rates</span>
        <span>Honest even when the answer is not software</span>
      </div>
    </section>



    <section class="cta-band reveal">
      <h2>Say it out loud, once.</h2>
      <p>A conversation in confidence costs nothing and usually settles who fits you — and if it isn’t us, we will tell you so.</p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content:center"><a class="btn" href={mailto}>Enquire in confidence <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <p class="contact-line">Direct: <a href="mailto:manuel@triarc.ch">manuel@triarc.ch</a></p>
    </section>

    <nav class="instrument-nav" aria-label="Triarc services">
      <a href="/en/">← Overview</a>
      <div class="links"><a href="/en/software">Software</a><a href="/en/beratung" aria-current="page">Consulting</a><a href="/en/recruiting">Recruiting</a></div>
    </nav>
  </main>
</Base>

<script>
  // The checklist writes the enquiry for you: whatever is ticked becomes the
  // body of a normal mailto. No form post, no storage, nothing leaves the
  // page until the visitor sends the mail themselves.
  const form = document.getElementById('check-form');
  const send = document.getElementById('check-send');
  const note = document.getElementById('check-count');
  if (form && send && note) {
    const base = send.getAttribute('href');
    const subject = send.dataset.subject;
    const intro = send.dataset.intro;
    const none = send.dataset.none;
    const emptyNote = note.textContent;
    const sync = () => {
      const picked = Array.from(form.querySelectorAll('input:checked')).map((i) => '- ' + i.value);
      if (!picked.length) {
        send.setAttribute('href', base);
        note.textContent = emptyNote;
        return;
      }
      const body = intro + '\n\n' + picked.join('\n') + '\n\nBetrieb:\n';
      send.setAttribute('href', 'mailto:manuel@triarc.ch?subject=' + encodeURIComponent(subject) + '&body=' + encodeURIComponent(body));
      note.textContent = picked.length === 1 ? '1 Punkt ausgewählt' : picked.length + ' Punkte ausgewählt';
    };
    form.addEventListener('change', sync);
    form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => e.preventDefault());
    sync();
  }
</script>


<style>
  /* the service names are longer words than Aurora/Nova/Zenith/Ceres,
     so the display size steps down to keep them inside the column */
  .d-h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 5.8vw, 74px); }

  /* the self-check: ticking is the whole interaction, so the boxes are the
     only new atom — a hairline square that takes the house diamond */
  .check-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 2px; background: var(--rule); border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .check-list li { background: var(--paper); }
  .check-list label { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 14px; padding: 18px 22px; cursor: pointer; transition: background 200ms ease; }
  .check-list label:hover { background: var(--accent-wash); }
  .check-list input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 0; height: 0; }
  .check-list .box { flex: none; width: 13px; height: 13px; margin-top: 3px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); position: relative; transition: border-color 200ms ease; }
  .check-list label:hover .box { border-color: var(--gold); }
  .check-list .box::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 2px; background: var(--gold); transform: rotate(45deg) scale(0); transition: transform 200ms var(--ease); }
  .check-list input:checked + .box::after { transform: rotate(45deg) scale(1); }
  .check-list input:focus-visible + .box { outline: 2px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .check-list .txt { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); }
  .check-foot { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 18px 24px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .check-note { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .check-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .check-list .box::after, .check-list label { transition: none; } }

</style>
